WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.389
You know what we all make mistakes,

00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.360
second chance I hope.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.040
I've been a good guy.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.320
As disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein
half-asses his way through sex addiction rehab,

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.799
more and more women, ranging from Oscar winner
Lupita Nyong’o,

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:16.660
to former teen star Molly Ringwald,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:22.000
keep coming forward with stories about his
abusive and sometimes criminal behavior.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.880
Even his brother and long time business partner
Bob Weinstein has disowned him

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.460
calling him indefensible, crazy and remorseless.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.570
But the Weinstein story is not just about
the end of a career,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.230
it's about the end of an era.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.840
The Miramax co-founder is only the latest
in a long line of powerful older men

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.180
whose professional lives have ended with revelations
of long term harassment and worse.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.280
Fox News cashiered it's founder, Roger Ailes
and star host Bill O'Reilly

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.740
because of similar charges.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.620
And Bill Cosby's 2014 comeback was destroyed
after claims surfaced

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.580
that he drugged and raped over a dozen women.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.640
The head of Amazon Studios was forced to resign
last week

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:04.409
after he was accused of repeatedly and insistently
propositioning

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:08.820
the producer of the streaming service's acclaimed
series 'The Man in the High Castle.'

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.520
Weinstein was widely and rightly derided for
blaming his decades long behavior

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.830
on 'having come of age in the 1960s
and 70s' he said

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.600
'when all the rules about behavior and workplaces
were different.'

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.500
Why don't you let me tape you?

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.260
Doing what?

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.040
Talking.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.420
About what?

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.180
About sex.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.180
Among other things, such a defense ignores
the inconvenient fact

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.160
that the 70s ended nearly four decades
ago.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.020
Today on the press and on the radio the American
career girl, married or single,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.330
is a favorite subject for discussion.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:44.760
But he is right that workplace expectations
have changed,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.120
and that's largely because the workplace itself
has changed,

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.520
About 60% of women are in the workforce

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.909
compared to just 43% in
1970.

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:57.920
In fact, more than half of all management,
professional and related positions

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.680
are held by women.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.360
The pay gap has also essentially vanished.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.340
A study of 33 countries including the United
States

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.840
found that when comparing workers doing the
same job

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.900
men made just 1.6% more than women.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.780
As I travel the world and represent our company,
I listen a lot.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.760
With higher pay, positions and status comes
more workplace power.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:26.980
My name is Victoria Valentino and I met Bill
Cosby in 1969, I was a folk singer-

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.130
I'm Louisa Moritz-

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.760
My name is Joyce Emmons-

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.740
Power that is amplified by social media

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.590
and other technologies that empower dissent

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.120
and make it harder and harder to maintain
a sexist status quo.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.220
He won the Heisman trophy with his DNA rape
kit.

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:48.239
There's a real issue that in the aftermath
of the Harvey Weinstein revelations,

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:51.120
behavior that is merely boorish or one time
only

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.100
will be conflated with systemic sexism and
far more reprehensible crimes.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.260
But surely it's more than coincidence

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:05.380
that the Weistein scandal broke just after
Hugh Hefner,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.769
the absolute personification of old-school
pre-equality male sexual identity,

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:12.910
was being lowered into the ground.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.090
The old days, and the old ways are being laid
to rest

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.829
and that's a very good thing for all of us
regardless of gender.

